ENTRY 11493 {"id":11493,"kind":"pi.tool-result","messages":[{"role":"toolResult","text":"packages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:17:import { createOrchestratorServer } from \"./http.js\";\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:32:  const server = createOrchestratorServer({\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:51:      await lifecycle.host?.close();\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:134:  lifecycle.host = host;\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:135:  lifecycle.service = service;\npackages/orchestrator/src/main.ts:136:  lifecycle.state = \"owner\";\npackages/orchestrator/src/sessions.ts:306:      \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleted', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1\",\npackages/orchestrator/src/sandboxes.ts:21:import { conversationOfName, interruptedExec, planSuspend } from \"./lifecycle.js\";\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts:48:export function createOrchestratorServer(deps: ServerDeps): Server {\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts:67:    sendJson(res, 200, { status: \"ok\", state: lifecycle.state, instance: lifecycle.instance });\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts:71:    const ready = lifecycle.host !== undefined && lifecycle.service !== undefined;\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts:72:    sendJson(res, ready ? 200 : 503, { state: lifecycle.state, instance: lifecycle.instance });\npackages/orchestrator/src/http.ts:85:    sendJson(res, 503, { error: lifecycle.state }, { \"retry-after\": \"2\" });\npackages/session-core/src/store.ts:167:export async function getSession(\npackages/session-core/src/store.ts:268:    \"update inbox.sessions set status = 'deleting', last_activity_at = clock_timestamp() where id = $1 and status in ('active', 'failed')\",\npackages/session-core/src/http.ts:3:export function sendJson(\n32:| `POST /sessions/{id}/events` body `{ kind, text?, sourceEventId? }` | `202 { eventId, duplicate }` | `kind` is `message`, `steer` or `cancel`. `text` is required for `message` and `steer` (at most 64 KiB). `sourceEventId` (at most 200 characters) deduplicates. `400` invalid body, `409` session is deleting or failed, or the id belongs to another session, `410` session deleted. |\n33:| `GET /sessions/{id}/stream` | `200 text/event-stream` | See Streaming. `503` with `Retry-After` while the orchestrator is down, `410` for a deleted session. |\n34:| `GET /sessions/{id}` | `200 { sessionId, status, model: { provider, model, reasoning? }, failure?, createdAt, lastActivityAt, events: { pending, submitted, failed } }` | Answered from Postgres, so it works while the orchestrator is down. `status` is `active`, `failed`, `deleting` or `deleted`; `failure` is present only when `failed`. A session that predates per-session models reports the default model. |\n69:  batch so later rows cannot overtake it. After 5 attempts (or at once for a permanent error such as a deleted\n86:| `deleted` | none | The session was deleted; the stream ends. |\n149:  right name and another or no label is refused, and never deleted by session deletion. (Claims that predate this\n179:`DELETE /sessions/{id}` answers `202` and queues a `delete` row. From that moment new events get `409` (`410` once deleted). Admission is one conditional insert (`session is active`), so an event whose body was still being read when the session was deleted is refused too, and the session is marked `deleting` before the delete row is written, so every accepted event sorts before it; events\n183:2. ends the session's open streams (`deleted`),\n185:4. marks the session `deleted` (`410` from then on).\n189:session is therefore marked deleted and its conversation rows stay in the `durable` schema until a maintenance job\n192:1. list `inbox.sessions where status = 'deleted' and conversation_id is not null`,\n197:That job is not implemented here. Until it runs, deleted sessions' transcripts remain in Postgres.\n203:after 5 attempts; a `delete` row has no attempt cap, because a failed delete leaves the session `deleting` with its\n204:sandbox, PVC and OneCLI agent alive, and the orphan sweep never touches a `deleting` session. A failing delete is\n206:`PermanentError` (the session row is gone or already `deleted`) ends the row `failed`. A repeated `DELETE` also puts a\n214:is `deleted` or has no row, and the object is older than `PI_SWEEP_GRACE_SECONDS` (600). At most `PI_SWEEP_MAX_ACTIONS`\n216:never touched, and neither is a session that is `active`, `failed` or `deleting`, even when its sandbox can no longer work.\n251:- Conversation state of deleted sessions stays until the maintenance job.\n","isError":false}]}
